{"id":"s5.1.6","slug":"inverse-trig","title":"Inverse Trigonometric Values","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Inverse trig answers are angles, and contest papers ask for them as a multiple of $\\pi$: \"$\\text{Arcsin}(x) = k\\pi$ radians, find $k$.\"</p><p class=\"mb-4\">Memorise the principal values. $\\text{Arcsin}$ returns angles in $[-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}]$; $\\text{Arccos}$ returns $[0, \\pi]$; $\\text{Arctan}$ returns $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2})$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For the reciprocal functions, convert first: $\\text{Arccsc}(x) = \\text{Arcsin}(1/x)$ and $\\text{Arcsec}(x) = \\text{Arccos}(1/x)$. So $\\text{Arccsc}(-2) = \\text{Arcsin}(-\\frac{1}{2}) = -\\frac{\\pi}{6}$, giving $k = -\\frac{1}{6}$.</p>","summary":"Inverse trig answers are angles, and contest papers ask for them as a multiple of : \" radians, find .\" Memorise the principal values.","generation_guideline":"Generate an inverse trig value question answered as a multiple of pi.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"$\\text{Arccsc}\\left(1\\right) = k\\pi$ radians. Find $k$.","answer":"1/2","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":2,"text":"$\\text{Arctan}\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right) = k\\pi$ radians. Find $k$.","answer":"-1/6","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":3,"text":"$\\text{Arccos}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = k\\pi$ radians. Find $k$.","answer":"1/3","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":4,"text":"$\\text{Arcsin}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) = k\\pi$ radians. Find $k$.","answer":"1/4","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":5,"text":"$\\text{Arcsin}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = k\\pi$ radians. Find $k$.","answer":"1/6","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":6,"text":"$\\text{Arctan}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right) = k\\pi$ radians. Find $k$.","answer":"1/6","kind":"exact","tags":["trigonometry"]},{"id":7,"text":"$\\text{Arccos}\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) = k\\pi$ radians. Find $k$.","answer":"5/6","kind":"exact","tags"